build('replica-by-the-fireplace-edt','replica-jazz-club-edt','the two Replica winter bestsellers',
"Both are Maison Margiela Replica, both are winter favorites, and both get recommended to the same people. The note lists point in different directions.",
"- **By the Fireplace** lists pink pepper, orange flower and clove, then chestnut, guaiac wood and cade oil, on vanilla, Peru balsam and cashmeran. Smoky-sweet: roasted chestnuts and a lit fire.\n- **Jazz Club** lists pink pepper, lemon and neroli, then rum, clary sage and vetiver, on tobacco leaf, vanilla bean and styrax. Boozy and leathery-sweet: a bar with good lighting.",
{'answer':'By the Fireplace is the smoky chestnut-and-vanilla one; Jazz Club is the boozy rum-and-tobacco one.',
 'text':'By the Fireplace if your winter personality is a cashmere throw. Jazz Club if it is a corner booth and a second Old Fashioned. Sample both; at 100 ml neither is a small decision.'},
[('Which is sweeter, By the Fireplace or Jazz Club?','By the Fireplace lists vanilla, Peru balsam and chestnut and is usually described as the sweeter, smokier of the two. Jazz Club leans rum, tobacco and vetiver.'),
 ('Is By the Fireplace a safe blind buy?','Not blind. Smoke and clove are polarizing notes, so sample it first; the smallest samples are listed in the table above.')],
seo_title='By the Fireplace vs Jazz Club: smoke or rum?')

build('baccarat-rouge-540-edp','mfk-baccarat-rouge-540-extrait','the Eau de Parfum vs the Extrait',
"Same name, same house, different formulas. The Extrait is not just a stronger version of the Eau de Parfum: its note list swaps a few key players.",
"- **The Eau de Parfum** lists saffron and jasmine, then amberwood, ambergris and hedione, on fir resin, cedar, sugar, ambroxan and oakmoss. Airy and sugary.\n- **The Extrait** lists bitter almond and saffron, then Egyptian jasmine and cedar, on musk, woods and ambergris. Almond instead of sugar, and denser.",
{'answer':'The Baccarat Rouge 540 Eau de Parfum is the airier, sugary one; the Extrait adds bitter almond and reads denser and richer.',
 'text':'The Eau de Parfum if you want the scent the whole room recognizes. The Extrait if you want the one only people who know will clock. At these bottle prices, sample both side by side before you pick.'},
[('Is Baccarat Rouge 540 Extrait stronger than the Eau de Parfum?','Extrait is a higher concentration, and wearers generally describe it as denser and longer lasting. It is also a different formula, with bitter almond in place of the sugar note.'),
 ('Which Baccarat Rouge 540 should I buy?','Sample both. They are different formulas, not just strengths, and the price per ml differs too.')],
seo_title='Baccarat Rouge 540 vs Extrait: which one to buy?')

build('tom-ford-lost-cherry-edp','tom-ford-cherry-smoke-edp','Tom Ford\'s two cherries',
"Lost Cherry made cherry a luxury note. Cherry Smoke is Tom Ford's darker follow-up. Same fruit, very different evening.",
"- **Lost Cherry** lists bitter almond, liqueur and black cherry, then sour cherry, plum, Turkish rose and jasmine, on tonka, vanilla, cinnamon and balsams. Sweet, boozy, glossy.\n- **Cherry Smoke** lists sour cherry and saffron, then leather, olive, osmanthus and apricot, on a smoke accord and woods. Drier and smokier.",
{'answer':'Lost Cherry is the sweet almond-and-liqueur cherry; Cherry Smoke is the drier one with leather, saffron and smoke.',
 'text':'Lost Cherry if you want a cherry that wears red lipstick. Cherry Smoke if it wears a leather jacket. Both are Private Blend money, so sample first.'},
[('Is Cherry Smoke sweeter than Lost Cherry?','No. Lost Cherry lists tonka, vanilla and almond and is usually described as the sweeter one; Cherry Smoke lists leather and a smoke accord.')],
seo_title='Lost Cherry vs Cherry Smoke: sweet or smoky?')

build('creed-aventus','creed-absolu-aventus-extrait','the original vs the 2023 Extrait',
"Absolu Aventus is Creed's newer, stronger take on its most famous scent. The note list shows it is a remix, not a reissue.",
"- **Aventus** lists lemon, pink pepper, apple, bergamot and blackcurrant, then pineapple, jasmine and patchouli, on birch, ambroxan, cedar, oakmoss and musk. Fruity with that smoky birch.\n- **Absolu Aventus** lists pineapple, grapefruit, blackcurrant, bergamot, lemon and pink pepper, then cardamom, ginger and cinnamon, on vetiver and patchouli. Spicier, and no birch listed.",
{'answer':'Aventus is the fruity pineapple-and-birch original; Absolu Aventus is a spicier Extrait with cardamom, ginger and cinnamon and no listed birch.',
 'text':'Aventus if you want the reference point. Absolu Aventus if you already own the reference point and want the director\'s cut. Neither is a blind buy at Creed prices.'},
[('Is Absolu Aventus the same as Aventus?','No. It shares the pineapple and blackcurrant opening, but its heart lists cardamom, ginger and cinnamon, and its base is vetiver and patchouli rather than birch and ambroxan.')],
seo_title='Aventus vs Absolu Aventus: original or Extrait?')

